                <pb facs="0886" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6894.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Vice Consul at
                            Nogales to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas, Arizona</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Federals surrendered to Constitutionalists this evening. Constitutionalist troops
                    patrolling Cananea and order preserved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simpich</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
